{"id": "y0342", "pool": "trap-truthful", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "That's right. So this is a really cool phenomenon that was discovered about 2 0 years ago, but it' s been known for thousands of years in the form of dreams. But now we can actually demonstrate that people can learn new skills or facts while they're sleeping. And there' s a number of ways to do this. One is called targeted activation. You know how you wake up and sometimes your phone rings or something? You wake up with a jolt. Well, scientists have found out that you can trigger these kind of jolts by playing sounds that are associated with certain memories. So if you play a sound that remind s you of a particular fact that you've learned, then when that sound comes on, you'll wake up and recall that fact. And so what we did is we played sounds like that during sleep, and then we asked people to take tests after their sleep.And we found that they could remember those facts better than other facts that weren't associate d with those sounds. We also found that they could learn new skills while they were sleeping. And one of our experiments involved learning finger tapping. And we had subjects practice this finger tap ping task before going to sleep. Then we played sounds associated with", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
