{"id": "y0966", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D, mutation. Mu tations are changes in the DNA sequence that can introduce new genetic variations into a population. These changes can be passed on to offspring and contribute significantly to genetic diversity. While processes like sporulation, binary f ission, and ve getative propagation can reproduce organisms, they typically do not introduce new genetic material unless combined with mutation or recombination.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
